#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:2
msgid "Snap components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:4
msgid ""
"Snap _components_ are parts of a snap that can be built and uploaded in "
"conjunction with a host snap and later optionally installed beside it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:6
msgid ""
"Components are useful for distributing optional resources for a snap, such "
"as debug symbols alongside snap binaries, and kernel modules alongside a "
"kernel snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:8
msgid ""
"Just like a snap, a component is implemented as a squashfs file. If "
"installed, this file is mounted in a location accessible to the host snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:10
msgid ""
"Components can be thought of as either an internal implementation detail of "
"the host snap that remains transparent to the user, or as a visible snap "
"component that can be installed, refreshed and removed similarly to snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:12
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Using components <how-to-guides-manage-snaps-using-components>` "
"for installation, removal and listing options. To manage components from "
"within a snap, see {ref}`snapctl <how-to-guides-manage-snaps-use-snapctl-"
"components>` components commands. Components can also be managed through the "
"[Snapd REST API](https://snapcraft.io/docs/reference/development/snapd-rest-"
"api/#/Asynchronous/manageSnaps)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:14
msgid "Component requires *snapd 2.67+* ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:16
msgid "Schema"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:18
msgid ""
"Components are defined with a top-level `components` keyword in a "
"snapcraft.yaml:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:20
msgid ""
"components:\n"
"  <name>:\n"
"    type: <standard|kernel-modules|...>\n"
"    summary: ...\n"
"    description: ...\n"
"  ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:29
msgid ""
"A corresponding `meta/component.yaml` file contains the metadata for each "
"component with the following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:31
msgid ""
"component: <snap_name>+<component_name>\n"
"type: <component_type>\n"
"version: <version>\n"
"summary: ...\n"
"description: ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:39
msgid "`component` and `type` are mandatory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:40
msgid "`version` will inherit the snap version if not set in component.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:42
msgid ""
"For more details on component types, see [Snapcraft components](https://"
"canonical-snapcraft.readthedocs-hosted.com/en/latest/reference/components/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:44
msgid ""
"It is possible to create a component by running `snap pack <dir>`, however, "
"`<dir>/meta/component.yaml` must already exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:46
msgid ""
"All files inside this directory will be included within the created squashfs "
"file, which will be named by default "
"`<snap_name>+<component_name>_<comp_version>.comp.`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:48
msgid ""
"For further details on packaging, see [Create a component](https://"
"documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/9.0/how-to/crafting/create-a-component/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:50
msgid "Revisions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:52
msgid ""
"Just like snaps, components have {ref}`revisions <explanation-how-snaps-work-"
"revisions>`. If a snap defines components, each snap file uploaded to the "
"store will be matched to components with their own specific revisions  This "
"forms a unique tuple between the snap and each respective component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:55
msgid ""
"ⓘ  While it will become possible to update components in a tuple, the "
"snapcraft functionality required to individually upload an updated component "
"has not yet been implemented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:57
msgid "Component hooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:59
msgid ""
"Components can implement the following  {ref}`hooks <reference-development-"
"supported-snap-hooks>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:61
msgid "install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:62
msgid "pre-refresh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:63
msgid "post-refresh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:64
msgid "remove"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:66
msgid ""
"These correspond to executables with the same name that must be stored in "
"meta/hooks/ inside the component file. Semantics will be similar as the "
"homonymous hooks for snaps, with the caveat that if run as part of the same "
"change that installs/refreshes/removes a snap, the following execution order "
"is defined:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:68
msgid "install hook: 1st snap’s, 2nd component’s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:69
msgid "pre-refresh hook: 1st component’s, 2nd snap’s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:70
msgid "post-refresh hook: 1st snap’s, 2nd component’s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:71
msgid "remove hook: 1st component’s, 2nd snap’s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:73
msgid ""
"The rationale for the order is that components have a dependency on the snap "
"and might need information from the snap to be present when installed. For "
"instance, we need the plug information that is part of the snap metadata "
"before we can run the component hook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:75
msgid ""
"The component hooks might need plugs. If that is the case, they need to be "
"defined in the snap metadata inside the snap container (as it is where we "
"have the capability to define plugs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:77
msgid ""
"The syntax in `snapcraft.yaml` and `snap.yaml` will be the same as for snap "
"hooks, but under the components.<name> stanza:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:77
msgid "<name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:79
msgid ""
"components:\n"
"  <name>:\n"
"    type: ...\n"
"    hooks:\n"
"      <hook_name>:\n"
"        plugs:\n"
"          - <plug_name>\n"
"          - ...\n"
"  ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:91
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:93
msgid ""
"The execution environment for component hooks will be similar to the one "
"defined for snap applications/hooks, with the injection of the following "
"additional {ref}`environment variables <reference-development-environment-"
"variables>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:95
msgid "`SNAP_COMPONENT`: directory where the component is mounted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:96
msgid ""
"`SNAP_COMPONENT_NAME`: name of the component as specified in component.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:97
msgid "`SNAP_COMPONENT_REVISION`: revision of the component"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:98
msgid ""
"`SNAP_COMPONENT_VERSION`: version of the component as specified in "
"component.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:100
msgid ""
"Component hooks run as confined snap applications, which is also the case "
"for all snap hooks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:102
msgid "Accessing components from within a snap environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-components.md:104
msgid ""
"Within the snap environment, all available components of the snap are "
"declared in `$SNAP/meta/snap.yaml`. All installed components are exposed "
"under `$SNAP_COMPONENTS/`, which is the same path as `$SNAP/../components/"
"$SNAP_REVISION/` used with _snapd_ older than 2.78. The content of each "
"component is available under `$SNAP_COMPONENTS/<comp-name>/` and the "
"presence of this non-empty directory indicates that a given component is "
"installed."
msgstr ""
